<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kongu Nadu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kongu Nadu is the historical region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, around the modern cities of Coimbatore, Erode, Salem and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karur">Karur</a>. A fertile upland crossed by trade routes between the east and west coasts, it was fought over by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chera-dynasty">Cheras</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a> and later Vijayanagara and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>. Finds of Roman coin hoards show its importance in ancient trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kongu-nadu.jpg" alt="Kongu Nadu" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C1MM original file: Chumwa · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kongu_Nadu_district_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
